Hello there,

I just finished my second ascension ever, and my first one on
nethack.alt.org. Nothing really spectacular here that would merit an
epic walkthrough, but just a couple of points to characterise the
game.

First off, I am used to the tiled Windows version (yeah, I know I'm a
wimp...), so it took a bit of getting used to the stone-age interface,
but not more than a couple of /-s were needed. I noticed that the
slightly annoying telnet lag forces you to slow down a bit which might
actually be not too bad a thing, so you don't risk running into danger
too much.

As usual, I went down in the main dungeon until I got Excalibur.
Alongside I found an elven mithril coat that allowed me to take on the
mines right away. My kitten did a good job but somehow got lost on the
way back. I stayed petless for the rest of the game. Sokoban had the
amulet of reflection, and DL 7 was a bones from a newbie wizard that
yielded a cloak of magic resistance. So I decided that in case I got a
wish, I would go for black dragon scale mail to get disintegration
resistance.

Lying in a corner I found Vorpal Blade (cursed of course) I "repaired"
an used it a little but after it was thorougly corroded from a black
pudding I decided to lock it away in a chest as my +5 Excalibur was
much more efficient. Of course I also sacrificed for Mj=F6llnir. The
quest was easy a usual when you're well-prepared. On the way further
down I found two amulets of live saving.

Two main features of the main dungeon were the lack of a bag of
holding (at least I got a sack in minetown) and the problems to get
all my stuff identified. I found only two ID scrolls that ID-ed only
wo items each. It was not a big help that I found two magic markers
along the way although I was lucky enough to get holy water quite
early so I could bless the markers. I must have written a least ten ?
oID until I got a full item list. The absence of a bag of holding made
it neccesary to build a few stashes and make a shuttle service between
altars which slowed the game a little. As BoH was top priority I dug
down through Medusa right to the castle. I was well prepared with
reasonable AC and ringa of levitaion and conflict. As always I entered
from behind and slayed the inhabitans at the back door. Found some
boots and gloves in the armor vault, turned out to be Water Walking
and GoD. Si I wished for BOH, GOP, speed boots and my BDSM. Itzchak
had only 2 candles, so to be on the safe side I wished for a bunch.

Having pumped up my AC to -25 I went on to Gehennom. The way down was
fairly easy, Jubilex was killed with three strokes (I never ever had
problem with this guy. Never was much harder to kill than a dust
vortex. Somewhere I read he wa suppused to be dangerous....) Vlad's
tower was conveniently located on the first possible level (in a
previous game the upstairs turned out to be underneath a boulder. I
searched for ages until i found it). Asmodeus teleported away, so I
decided to leave him for now. Orcus was no problem either. No fake
wizard's tower this time, my =3DoC took care of the bestiary. Rodney
gave away the book of the dead after only a little melee. Bottom level
happened to be just underneath the wizard's tower, it took a while to
find the vibrating square. After fighting my way halfway through the
sanctum with a little help from a cockatrice corpse and the =3DoC I was
greeted by Yeenoghu and Demorgorgon simultaneously It helped that they
keep teleporting away after a hit, so I never really was in danger. My
210 HP hardly went below 180. Demogrgon was surpisingly easy to defeat
(never met him before). Of course he came with his sickness attacks,
but my blessed unicorn horm worked reliably. Yeenoghu was a bit more
of a pest. In the temple I found the corpse of the high priest but no
amulet. It must have been stolen by Yeenoghu, and so it was. I
finished him on the level above. I made my last wish for scrolls of
genocide to get rid of the arch-lich repeatedly calling nasties.

On the way up, Rodney's incarnations were far tougher than the first
kill, an I actualy had to use one of the amulets of life saving.
Interestingly I was never hit by the mysterious force. For a few
levels I was accompanied by Asmodeus and Baalzebub. They were no real
threat but slowed down the pace a bit. Plane of earth was easy, I
located the portal with the last charge of the Orb. It happened to be
in the neighbouring cavern, so two zaps of the wand of digging were
enough. Also the other planes were not too tough with both rings of
levitation and conflict worn. Two of the remaining portals were
disclosed by monsters activating them.

On the Astral Plane things got a bit tougher. Death was easy to kill a
couple of times but managed drain my max HP a bit. Leftmost altar
turned out to be Odin, guarded by Death, in the center was Tyr,
guarded by Famine who was a piece of cake. I did not come into contact
with Pestilence who must have been hanging around Loki's altar. I
smashed my way through the altar, removed my =3DoC so my high proest
wouldn't attack me, and offered the amulet. Game over.

One thing to note: I practiced with Mj=F6llnir to get the skill to
expert, but I never used it it afterwards. The entire game from the
quest to the end I wielded only Excalibur, originally +5, reduced to
+4 by a disenchanter on the way up. Worked just fine.

My next tries will be to ascend a spellcaster. I have tried wizards
and priests en masse, but I rarely reached Gehennom so far.

Hope you enjoyed it,
